/-!
# Intrinsic block exclusions for the binary parabolics

In dimension five, the two radicals of each paired flag are abelian,
normal, and self-centralizing, and their intersection is generated by
cross commutators. The genuine C.1.7 irreducibility and two-perfection
conditions therefore exclude every short subnormal embedding. This
covers both the 1+3+1 and the 2+1+2 flag, including its cubic Levi factors.

In dimension four, either end parabolic has actual two-core quotient
GL₃(2). Subnormality makes a candidate's image in this simple quotient
trivial or surjective. The short-group quotient calculation identifies
its quotient by O₂ with GL₃(2), whose order 168 excludes every C.1.12
chi-zero type. The block remains the original domain of the embedding.

The radical-pair argument reuses the checked Chapter 2 middle-flag
criterion. The end-quotient coordinates adapt the calculation in
Chapter13/.../Parabolics/Levi/FourComponent/Flags.lean to the published
Theory cut spaces, using the actual block action and its proved kernel.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), E.6.8,
printed pp.247–248, and C.1.7/C.1.12, printed pp.123–124.
-/

public section

